ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\ud83d\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True`\n\n\ud83d\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True`\r\n\r\nRelated to https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/14184, https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/14483\r\n\r\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_fastapi_14482.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for fastapi_14482 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom fastapi._compat.v2 import ModelField  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True` \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True` Related to https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussi...\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", ModelField)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "File written."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_14482.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "FAIL: \ud83d\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True` \ud83d\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True` Related to https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussi..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/_compat/v2.py (hunk at line 1).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/_compat/v2.py\", \"old_text\": \"import re\\nimport warnings\\nfrom copy import copy, deepcopy\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom enum import Enum\\nfrom typing import (\\n    Any,\", \"new_text\": \"import re\\nimport warnings\\nfrom copy import copy, deepcopy\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, is_dataclass\\nfrom enum import Enum\\nfrom typing import (\\n    Any,\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/_compat/v2.py (hunk at line 18).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/_compat/v2.py\", \"old_text\": \"from fastapi._compat import may_v1, shared\\nfrom fastapi.openapi.constants import REF_TEMPLATE\\nfrom fastapi.types import IncEx, ModelNameMap, UnionType\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, TypeAdapter, create_model\\nfrom pydantic import PydanticSchemaGenerationError as PydanticSchemaGenerationError\\nfrom pydantic import PydanticUndefinedAnnotation as PydanticUndefinedAnnotation\\nfrom pydantic import ValidationError as ValidationError\", \"new_text\": \"from fastapi._compat import may_v1, shared\\nfrom fastapi.openapi.constants import REF_TEMPLATE\\nfrom fastapi.types import IncEx, ModelNameMap, UnionType\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, TypeAdapter, create_model\\nfrom pydantic import PydanticSchemaGenerationError as PydanticSchemaGenerationError\\nfrom pydantic import PydanticUndefinedAnnotation as PydanticUndefinedAnnotation\\nfrom pydantic import ValidationError as ValidationError\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_14482", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "71a17b5932e38bcf798fcd05c5bb384e6d4db5bf", "files": ["fastapi/_compat/v2.py"], "symbols": ["ModelField", "alias", "__post_init__", "get_default"], "n_hunks": 5, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_arbitrary_types.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "tes