       See also: https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/nn.functional.html#interpolate\n   381\t            align_corners: This only has an effect when mode is\n   382\t                'linear', 'bilinear', 'bicubic' or 'trilinear'. Defaults to ``self.align_corners``.\n   383\t                See also: https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/nn.functional.html#interpolate\n   384\t\n   385\t        Raises:\n   386\t            ValueError: When ``self.spatial_size`` length is less than ``img`` spatial dimensions.\n   387\t\n   388\t        \"\"\"\n   389\t        if self.size_mode == \"all\":\n   390\t            input_ndim = img.ndim - 1  # spatial ndim\n   391\t            output_ndim = len(ensure_tuple(self.spatial_size))\n   392\t            if output_ndim > input_ndim:\n   393\t                input_shape = ensure_tuple_size(img.shape, output_ndim + 1, 1)\n   394\t                img = img.reshape(input_shape)\n   395\t            elif output_ndim < input_ndim:\n   396\t                raise ValueError(\n   397\t                    \"len(spatial_size) must be greater or equal to img spatial dimensions, \"\n   398\t                    f\"got spatial_size={output_ndim} img={input_ndim}.\"\n   399\t                )\n   400\t            spatial_size_ = fall_back_tuple(self.spatial_size, img.shape[1:])\n   401\t        else:  # for the \"longest\" mode\n   402\t            img_size = img.shape[1:]\n   403\t            if not isinstance(self.spatial_size, int):\n   404\t                raise ValueError(\"spatial_size must be an i\n[... observation truncated ...]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The problem is indeed related to floating-point inaccuracies in the calculation of `spatial_size_` when using the \"longest\" size mode. The line responsible for this is:\n```python\nspatial_size_ = tuple(ceil(s * scale) for s in img_size)\n```\n\nTo address the issue, I can replace `ceil` with `round`, ensuring the calculation produces the correct output size by rounding to the nearest integer, reducing errors due to floating point arithmetic.\n\nLet's apply this change.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/Project-MONAI__MONAI__0.6/monai/transforms/spatial/array.py\", \"old_text\": \"spatial_size_ = tuple(ceil(s * scale) for s in img_size)\", \"new_text\": \"spatial_size_ = tuple(round(s * scale) for s in img_size)\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "swegym-sft", "instance_id": "unknown", "traj_turn": 9, "tool": "edit_file", "est_tokens": 1502}}
