rator)s would cause urllib3 to attempt to reparse the request-uri as a full URI with a host and port. This bypasses that logic in ConnectionPool.urlopen by replacing these leading /s with just a single /.\r\n\r\nCloses #6643"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll localize with the graph tools first, starting from the symbols named in the issue.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"search_similar_code\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"request_url\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"request_url\",\n \"matches\": [\n  {\n   \"file\": \"src/requests/adapters.py\",\n   \"line\": 369,\n   \"kind\": \"definition\"\n  }\n ]\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "request_url is defined in src/requests/adapters.py. Checking its callers and callees before reading any file.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_neighbors\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"request_url\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"request_url\",\n \"callers\": [\n  \"startswith\",\n  \"lstrip\"\n ],\n \"callees\": [\n  \"startswith\",\n  \"lstrip\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"neighbors derived from symbols co-occurring in the patch\"\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Getting the surrounding call graph so I read only the files that matter.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_subgraph\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"request_url\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "requests_6644", "repo": "psf/requests", "base_commit": "382fc2c0c6c0ef0874bc65bc1175f97c073e5086", "files": ["src/requests/adapters.py"], "symbols": ["request_url", "startswith", "lstrip"], "n_hunks": 1, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_adapters.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the 