ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Test on urllib3 1.26.x\n\nFirst step to address #6734. We'll enable testing on urllib3 1.26.x which was lost when we moved the pin to support 2.x. These will fail for now until the underlying issue is addressed, but this is to ensure we're catching any future breakages."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_requests_6757.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "FAIL: Test on urllib3 1.26.x First step to address #6734. We'll enable testing on urllib3 1.26.x which was lost when we moved the pin to support 2.x. These will fail for now until the underlying issue is ad..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in src/requests/compat.py (hunk at line 10).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"src/requests/compat.py\", \"old_text\": \"import importlib\\nimport sys\\n\\n# -------------------\\n# Character Detection\\n# -------------------\", \"new_text\": \"import importlib\\nimport sys\\n\\n# -------\\n# urllib3\\n# -------\\nfrom urllib3 import __version__ as urllib3_version\\n\\n# Detect which major version of urllib3 is being used.\\ntry:\\n    is_urllib3_1 = int(urllib3_version.split(\\\".\\\")[0]) == 1\\nexcept (TypeError, AttributeError):\\n    # If we can't discern a version, prefer old functionality.\\n    is_urllib3_1 = True\\n\\n# -------------------\\n# Character Detection\\n# -------------------\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in src/requests/utils.py (hunk at line 38).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"src/requests/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"    getproxies,\\n    getproxies_environment,\\n    integer_types,\\n)\\nfrom .compat import parse_http_list as _parse_list_header\\nfrom .compat import (\", \"new_text\": \"    getproxies,\\n    getproxies_environment,\\n    integer_types,\\n    is_urllib3_1,\\n)\\nfrom .compat import parse_http_list as _parse_list_header\\nfrom .compat import (\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in src/requests/utils.py (hunk at line 137).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"src/requests/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"    total_length = None\\n    current_position = 0\\n\\n    if isinstance(o, str):\\n        o = o.encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n    if hasattr(o, \\\"__len__\\\"):\", \"new_text\": \"    total_length = None\\n    current_position = 0\\n\\n    if not is_urllib3_1 and isinstance(o, str):\\n        # urllib3 2.x+ treats all strings as utf-8 instead\\n        # of latin-1 (iso-8859-1) like http.client.\\n        o = o.encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n    if hasattr(o, \\\"__len__\\\"):\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Re-running the repro after the edit to check the fix.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_requests_6757.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "PASS: repro script now succeeds (no failure output after the fix)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Repro passes. Now the narrowest relevant tests.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python -m pytest tests/test_requests.py -q\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "PASS: pytest tests/test_requests.py \u2014 all collected tests passed after the fix."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Tests pass. Confirming the diff touches only library code before submitting.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_status\", \"arguments\": {}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "git status --short:\n modified: src/requests/compat.py\n modified: src/requests/utils.py\n modified: src/requests/utils.py\n(diff touches library code only; no test/config files)"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Fix verified 