{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "# Coder \u2014 system prompt\n\nYou are an offline autonomous Python coding agent working in /workspace, a\nrepository snapshot at the commit just before the fix. You resolve one\nissue per session: diagnose the bug or feature request, write the\nsmallest patch that makes the hidden tests pass, and submit it.\n\nThe hidden tests are applied AFTER your patch in a clean container. Test\nfiles and runner config are reset there, so editing them here is wasted\nwork and stripped from your patch. Fix library code only.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n- NEVER edit, create, or delete test files or runner config: tests,\n  conftest, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml, tox.ini, setup.cfg, and any\n  packaging or test-runner file. If a fix seems to need a test change,\n  you are wrong: re-read the issue and the library code.\n- NEVER write scratch scripts, repro scripts, or temp files under\n  /workspace: anything left there enters the patch diff. Scratch work\n  goes under /tmp only, and is deleted before submit.\n- Minimal patches only: change the fewest lines that fix the issue,\n  preserve existing style and names, do not refactor, do not add\n  features the issue does not ask for.\n- Never guess an API or symbol: read the code first.\n- Do not browse the network: there is none. All tools are offline.\n\n## Workflow (follow in order, do not skip steps)\n\n1. READ THE TASK. Extract: what fails, the exact error or wrong\n   behaviour, and any failing test names mentioned in the issue.\n2. LOCALIZE (graph first). Call the code_analyzer sub-agent once with\n   the issue text and the failing test names. Then use the graph tools\n   yourself on the SYMBOLS it returns (never natural-language queries):\n   search_similar_code for symbol lookup, get_code_neighbors for\n   callers and callees, get_code_subgraph for the surrounding call\n   graph. Only then read_file the 1-3 files that matter. Skim, do not\n   dump whole files: read_file returns at most 150 lines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\ud83d\udc1b Fix support for tagged union with discriminator inside of `Annotated` with `Body()`\n\n\ud83d\udc1b Fix support for tagged union with discriminator inside of `Annotated` with `Body()`\r\n\r\nRelated to: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/14495, https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/14508"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/_compat/v2.py (hunk at line 50).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/_compat/v2.py\", \"old_text\": \"evaluate_forwardref = eval_type_lenient\\nValidator = Any\\n\\n\\nclass BaseConfig:\\n    pass\", \"new_text\": \"evaluate_forwardref = eval_type_lenient\\nValidator = Any\\n\\n# TODO: remove when dropping support for Pydantic < v2.12.3\\n_Attrs = {\\n    \\\"default\\\": ...,\\n    \\\"default_factory\\\": None,\\n    \\\"alias\\\": None,\\n    \\\"alias_priority\\\": None,\\n    \\\"validation_alias\\\": None,\\n    \\\"serialization_alias\\\": None,\\n    \\\"title\\\": None,\\n    \\\"field_title_generator\\\": None,\\n    \\\"description\\\": None,\\n    \\\"examples\\\": None,\\n    \\\"exclude\\\": None,\\n    \\\"exclude_if\\\": None,\\n    \\\"discriminator\\\": None,\\n    \\\"deprecated\\\": None,\\n    \\\"json_schema_extra\\\": None,\\n    \\\"frozen\\\": None,\\n    \\\"validate_default\\\": None,\\n    \\\"repr\\\": True,\\n    \\\"init\\\": None,\\n    \\\"init_var\\\": None,\\n    \\\"kw_only\\\": None,\\n}\\n\\n\\n# TODO: remove when dropping support for Pydantic < v2.12.3\\ndef asdict(field_info: FieldInfo) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\n    attributes = {}\\n    for attr in _Attrs:\\n        value = getattr(field_info, attr, Undefined)\\n        if value is not Undefined:\\n            attributes[attr] = value\\n    return {\\n        \\\"annotation\\\": field_info.annotation,\\n        \\\"metadata\\\": field_info.metadata,\\n        \\\"attributes\\\": attributes,\\n    }\\n\\n\\nclass BaseConfig:\\n    pass\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/_compat/v2.py (hunk at line 134).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/_compat/v2.py\", \"old_text\": \"                warnings.simplefilter(\\n                    \\\"ignore\\\", category=UnsupportedFieldAttributeWarning\\n                )\\n            annotated_args = (\\n                self.field_info.annotation,\\n                *self.field_info.metadata,\\n                self.field_info,\\n            )\\n            self._type_adapter: TypeAdapter[Any] = TypeAdapter(\\n                Annotated[annotated_args],\", \"new_text\": \"                warnings.simplefilter(\\n                    \\\"ignore\\\", category=UnsupportedFieldAttributeWarning\\n                )\\n            # TODO: remove after dropping support for Python 3.8 and\\n            # setting the min Pydantic to v2.12.3 that adds asdict()\\n            field_dict = asdict(self.field_info)\\n            annotated_args = (\\n                field_dict[\\\"annotation\\\"],\\n                *field_dict[\\\"metadata\\\"],\\n                # this FieldInfo needs to be created again so that it doesn't include\\n                # the old field info metadata and only the rest of the attributes\\n                Field(**field_dict[\\\"attributes\\\"]),\\n            )\\n            self._type_adapter: TypeAdapter[Any] = TypeAdapter(\\n                Annotated[annotated_args],\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Re-running the repro after the edit to check the fix.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_14512.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "PASS: repro script now succeeds (no failure output after the fix)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Repro passes. Now the narrowest relevant tests.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python -m pytest tests/