ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\ud83d\udc1b Fix support for `StreamingResponse`s with dependencies with `yield` or `UploadFile`s, close after the response is done\n\n\ud83d\udc1b Fix support for `StreamingResponse`s with dependencies with `yield` or `UploadFile`s, close after the response is done\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThere's (again) an `AsyncExitStack` middleware, now used mainly to close objects after the response is done.\r\n\r\nThere's also a new wrapper duplicating some logic in Starlette but creating an `AsyncExitStack` for the exit code in dependencies with `yield`, for regular responses and WebSockets as well.\r\n\r\nThe exit code of dependencies with `yield` is now executed after the response is done."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/middleware/asyncexitstack.py (hunk at line 1).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/middleware/asyncexitstack.py\", \"old_text\": \"\", \"new_text\": \"from contextlib import AsyncExitStack\\n\\nfrom starlette.types import ASGIApp, Receive, Scope, Send\\n\\n\\n# Used mainly to close files after the request is done, dependencies are closed\\n# in their own AsyncExitStack\\nclass AsyncExitStackMiddleware:\\n    def __init__(\\n        self, app: ASGIApp, context_name: str = \\\"fastapi_middleware_astack\\\"\\n    ) -> None:\\n        self.app = app\\n        self.context_name = context_name\\n\\n    async def __call__(self, scope: Scope, receive: Receive, send: Send) -> None:\\n        async with AsyncExitStack() as stack:\\n            scope[self.context_name] = stack\\n            await self.app(scope, receive, send)\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/routing.py (hunk at line 1).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/routing.py\", \"old_text\": \"import dataclasses\\nimport email.message\\nimport inspect\\nimport json\\nimport sys\", \"new_text\": \"import dataclasses\\nimport email.message\\nimport functools\\nimport inspect\\nimport json\\nimport sys\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/routing.py (hunk at line 9).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/routing.py\", \"old_text\": \"from typing import (\\n    Any,\\n    AsyncIterator,\\n    Callable,\\n    Collection,\\n    Coroutine,\", \"new_text\": \"from typing import (\\n    Any,\\n    AsyncIterator,\\n    Awaitable,\\n    Callable,\\n    Collection,\\n    Coroutine,\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/routing.py (hunk at line 61).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/routing.py\", \"old_text\": \")\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\\nfrom starlette import routing\\nfrom starlette.concurrency import run_in_threadpool\\nfrom starlette.exceptions import HTTPException\\nfrom starlette.requests import Request\", \"new_text\": \")\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\\nfrom starlette import routing\\nfrom starlette._exception_handler import wrap_app_handling_exceptions\\nfrom starlette._utils import is_async_callable\\nfrom starlette.concurrency import run_in_threadpool\\nfrom starlette.exceptions import HTTPException\\nfrom starlette.requests import Request\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_14099", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "861b22c40897a03d2d7e5926923d962121ed5e2e", "files": ["docs_src/dependencies/tutorial013_an_py310.py", "docs_src/dependencies/tutorial014_an_py310.py", "fastapi/applications.py", "fastapi/middleware/asyncexitstack.py", "fastapi/routing.py"], "symbols": ["User", "get_session", "get_user", "generate_stream"], "n_hunks": 13, "n_files": 5, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 3, "test_target": ["tests/test_dependency_after_yield_raise.py", "tests/test_dependency_after_yield_streaming.py"], "test_target_