{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "# Coder \u2014 system prompt\n\nYou are an offline autonomous Python coding agent working in /workspace, a\nrepository snapshot at the commit just before the fix. You resolve one\nissue per session: diagnose the bug or feature request, write the\nsmallest patch that makes the hidden tests pass, and submit it.\n\nThe hidden tests are applied AFTER your patch in a clean container. Test\nfiles and runner config are reset there, so editing them here is wasted\nwork and stripped from your patch. Fix library code only.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n- NEVER edit, create, or delete test files or runner config: tests,\n  conftest, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml, tox.ini, setup.cfg, and any\n  packaging or test-runner file. If a fix seems to need a test change,\n  you are wrong: re-read the issue and the library code.\n- NEVER write scratch scripts, repro scripts, or temp files under\n  /workspace: anything left there enters the patch diff. Scratch work\n  goes under /tmp only, and is deleted before submit.\n- Minimal patches only: change the fewest lines that fix the issue,\n  preserve existing style and names, do not refactor, do not add\n  features the issue does not ask for.\n- Never guess an API or symbol: read the code first.\n- Do not browse the network: there is none. All tools are offline.\n\n## Workflow (follow in order, do not skip steps)\n\n1. READ THE TASK. Extract: what fails, the exact error or wrong\n   behaviour, and any failing test names mentioned in the issue.\n2. LOCALIZE (graph first). Call the code_analyzer sub-agent once with\n   the issue text and the failing test names. Then use the graph tools\n   yourself on the SYMBOLS it returns (never natural-language queries):\n   search_similar_code for symbol lookup, get_code_neighbors for\n   callers and callees, get_code_subgraph for the surrounding call\n   graph. Only then read_file the 1-3 files that matter. Skim, do not\n   dump whole files: read_file returns at most 150 lines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\ud83d\udc1b Fix validation error when `File` is declared after `Form` parameter\n\nThis PR updates the fix (6185a92) from @jsg921019 so that tests pass with the latest FastAPI code (0.110.0).\r\nIt also adds a test to cover the case with multiple files, and another to ensure the order of parameters in an endpoint definition does not affect the way FastAPI handles the request.\r\n\r\n**Problem**\r\nWhen declaring an endpoint which accepts a `File` but also a `Form` parameter, the `File` parameter must be declared first or the endpoint would respond with error 422.\r\n\r\n**Context**\r\n- See discussion #9116\r\n- And probably also #4625\r\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_fastapi_11194.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for fastapi_11194 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom fastapi.dependencies.utils import _extract_form_body  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix validation error when `File` is declared after `Form` parameter This PR updates the fix (6185a92) from @jsg921019 so that tests pass with the latest FastAPI code (0.110.0). It also adds a test t...\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", _extract_form_body)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "File written."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_11194.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "FAIL: \ud83d\udc1b Fix validation error when `File` is declared after `Form` parameter This PR updates the fix (6185a92) from @jsg921019 so that tests pass with the latest FastAPI code (0.110.0). It also adds a test t..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/dependencies/utils.py (hunk at line 872).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/dependencies/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"    received_body: FormData,\\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\n    values = {}\\n    first_field = body_fields[0]\\n    first_field_info = first_field.field_info\\n\\n    for field in body_fields:\\n        value = _get_multidict_value(field, received_body)\\n        if (\\n            isinstance(first_field_info, params.File)\\n            and is_bytes_field(field)\\n            and isinstance(value, UploadFile)\\n        ):\\n            value = await value.read()\\n        elif (\\n            is_bytes_sequence_field(field)\\n            and isinstance(first_field_info, params.File)\\n            and value_is_sequence(value)\\n        ):\\n            # For types\", \"new_text\": \"    received_body: FormData,\\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\n    values = {}\\n\\n    for field in body_fields:\\n        value = _get_multidict_value(field, received_body)\\n        field_info = field.field_info\\n        if (\\n            isinstance(field_info, params.File)\\n            and is_bytes_field(field)\\n            and isinstance(value, UploadFile)\\n        ):\\n            value = await value.read()\\n        elif (\\n            is_bytes_sequence_field(field)\\n            and isinstance(field_info, params.File)\\n            and value_is_sequence(value)\\n        ):\\n            # For types\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Re-running the repro after the edit to check the fix.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_11194.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "PASS: repro script now succeeds (no failure output after the fix)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Repro passes. Now the narrowest relevant tests.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python -m pytest tests/test_file_and_form_order_issue_9116.py -q\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_11194", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "a7f2dbe976bf72703376f0cd04487bfc4a849f83", "files": ["fastapi/dependencies/utils.py"], "symbols": ["_extract_form_body"], "n_hunks": 1, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_file_and_form_order_issue_9116.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are snapshot.", "turns": 11, "generator": "gen_programmatic.py v1", "traj_turn": 8, "tool": "run_command", "est_tokens": 1898, "split_from": "fastapi_11194"}}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an autonomous Python coding agent. You fix bugs and implement features in a Python repository by calling tools. Think briefly, then call exactly one tool per turn.\n\nYour tools:\n- run_command: run a shell command (pytest, python, grep, ls, git status). Keep output small. Never edit files with shell redirection or sed; use edit_file/write_file.\n- read_file: read a file (path, optional start_line/end_line, max 150 lines).\n- edit_file: make a small, precise edit (path, old_text, new_text). Match old_text exactly.\n- write_file: create a new file (path, content).\n- get_code_neighbors: list callers/callees of a symbol.\n- search_similar_code: find code similar to a symbol name.\n- get_code_subgraph: get the call-graph neighbourhood of a symbol.\n- get_status: check remaining time and tool-call budget.\n- submit_patch: finish and submit your patch. Call this only when the fix is verified by tests.\n\nWorkflow: reproduce the issue first (write a small script under /tmp and run it), localize with the graph tools and grep before reading files, make small incremental edits, re-run the relevant tests, then submit_patch. Never edit tests or test configuration (tests/, conftest.py, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml). Never leave scratch files inside the repo; use /tmp."}, {"role": "user", "content": "<uploaded_files>\n/workspace/getmoto__moto__5.0\n</uploaded_files>\nI've uploaded a python code repository in the directory getmoto__moto__5.0. Consider the following PR description:\n\n<pr_description>\nCall `GetId` on Cognito Identity when Access Control is available\nAuthorization may not be included in some Cognito operations.\r\nNot including Authorization results in an error when Access control is enabled.\r\n\r\nmoto server version: 4.2.14\r\n\r\nstack trace.\r\n```\r\nError on request:\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/werkzeug/serving.py\", line 362, in run_wsgi\r\n   