{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an autonomous Python coding agent. You fix bugs and implement features in a Python repository by calling tools. Think briefly, then call exactly one tool per turn.\n\nYour tools:\n- run_command: run a shell command (pytest, python, grep, ls, git status). Keep output small. Never edit files with shell redirection or sed; use edit_file/write_file.\n- read_file: read a file (path, optional start_line/end_line, max 150 lines).\n- edit_file: make a small, precise edit (path, old_text, new_text). Match old_text exactly.\n- write_file: create a new file (path, content).\n- get_code_neighbors: list callers/callees of a symbol.\n- search_similar_code: find code similar to a symbol name.\n- get_code_subgraph: get the call-graph neighbourhood of a symbol.\n- get_status: check remaining time and tool-call budget.\n- submit_patch: finish and submit your patch. Call this only when the fix is verified by tests.\n\nWorkflow: reproduce the issue first (write a small script under /tmp and run it), localize with the graph tools and grep before reading files, make small incremental edits, re-run the relevant tests, then submit_patch. Never edit tests or test configuration (tests/, conftest.py, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml). Never leave scratch files inside the repo; use /tmp."}, {"role": "user", "content": "<uploaded_files>\n/workspace/getmoto__moto__4.1\n</uploaded_files>\nI've uploaded a python code repository in the directory getmoto__moto__4.1. Consider the following PR description:\n\n<pr_description>\nSNS topics on incorrect region unexpectedly succeeds\n## Reporting Bugs\r\n\r\nDear `moto` team, I am wondering if this is the expected behaviour but it seems the behaviour changed recently (`4.0.11` vs `4.1.10`, always installed with `pip`).\r\nI am creating a topic in a region and trying to load it in another region. I was expecting this fail which was the case in 4.0.11\r\n\r\nStep to reproduce:\r\n\r\n```\r\nregion = \"us-east-1